                <pb facs="0373" n="293" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg293"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Hart</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-03-26"><hi rendition="#italic">March 26,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 385.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose copy of a letter from the board
                    of foreign missions of the Presbyterian Church in the United States protesting
                    against the action of the governor of Barranquilla in closing a boys’ school in
                    that city conducted under the auspices of that board.</p>
                <p>You will report what you have done and what can be done to secure to the
                    missionaries sent by this board all the rights they may have under the treaties
                    between the United States and Colombia.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay</hi>.</signed></closer>












